## Configurable Databricks button styles: Create (filled) and Share (outlined)
================================================================================

Context: The Databricks Catalog browse page uses two button styles: Create
(solid primary) and Share (outlined secondary). OntoBricks now exposes both in
Settings → Configuration → UI → Theme, defaulting to the Databricks values and
letting an admin change the colours. Applied to page buttons (`.btn-primary` =
Create, `.btn-secondary` / `.btn-outline-secondary` = Share) and to the navbar
chrome: Save = Create, Close = Share, Resume editing stays a warning ghost.
Blank or invalid stored colours fall back to the Databricks defaults.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/helpers/UIBranding.py
   - `DEFAULT_BUTTON_PRIMARY_COLOR` (#2272B4) and `DEFAULT_BUTTON_SECONDARY_COLOR`
     (#11171C); Databricks companion tints (`DATABRICKS_CREATE_HOVER`,
     `DATABRICKS_SHARE_BORDER`, `DATABRICKS_SHARE_HOVER`) used exactly for defaults.
   - `BrandPalette` gains `button_primary`, `button_primary_hover`,
     `button_on_primary`, `button_secondary`, `button_secondary_border`,
     `button_secondary_hover`; `UIBranding` gains `button_primary_color` and
     `button_secondary_color`.
   - New `derive_button_palette()`; `derive_brand_palette()` and
     `normalize_ui_branding()` accept and resolve the two colours.
