## Du Bois md geometry for page buttons (Create/Share look on every CTA)
================================================================================

Context: Create/Share colour tokens were applied, but page buttons (e.g.
Context → Versions) still looked Bootstrap-native: auto height, 2px radius,
14px / weight 400. Databricks Catalog Create/Share use Du Bois md geometry
(32px, 4px, 13px / 500). Page CTAs now share that geometry with the navbar
chrome.

Root cause: `components.css` only restyled colour on `.btn-*` variants; the
base `.btn` / `.btn-sm` size ramp was still Bootstrap's.

Changes:

1. src/front/static/global/css/main.css
   - Added `--db-btn-height` (2rem), `--db-btn-radius` (0.25rem),
     `--db-btn-font-size` (0.8125rem), `--db-btn-font-weight` (500),
     `--db-btn-padding-x` (0.75rem).
   - Navbar chrome tokens `--ob-subnav-btn-*` now alias those values.
   - Input-group / btn-group size ramps: form fields keep `--db-radius-control`;
     buttons use `--db-btn-radius`. Section-header wrapped groups use the
     button radius.
2. src/front/static/global/css/components.css
   - `.btn` / `.btn-sm` / `.btn-lg` use Du Bois md geometry (inline-flex,
     fixed height, 13px/500, 4px radius). `.btn-link` and `.btn-close` are
     excluded from that ramp.
3. .cursor/11-frontend-design.mdc
   - Documents the shared button geometry tokens.
4. tests/units/front/test_button_design_contract.py
   - Button radius assertions use `--db-btn-radius`; form fields stay on
     `--db-radius-control`.
5. tests/units/front/test_segmented_subnav_contract.py
   - Chrome height/radius assert the alias to `--db-btn-*`.
6. tests/units/front/test_ui_button_styles_contract.py
   - New contract for Du Bois md geometry tokens and `.btn` usage.

