## Speed up Context open (skip sims/OWL, paint chrome early)
================================================================================

Context: Opening a Context felt slow even with the loading spinner. Root
causes: every load-from-uc attached up to 500 simulation runs (never imported
into the session), eagerly regenerated OWL/R2RML that save() immediately
strips, double session saves, artificial 150 ms navigate delays, and the UI
waiting on /navbar/state before Save/Close appeared.

Changes:

1. src/back/objects/domain/Domain.py
   Lean load_domain_from_uc: include_simulations=False, no
   ensure_generated_content, single save; return domain payload for chrome;
   extract _resolve_uc_load_version / _commit_uc_load_session helpers.
2. src/back/objects/registry/store/lakebase/Catalog.py
   read_version(include_simulations=…) skips attach_simulations_to_doc when False.
3. src/back/objects/registry/store/base.py + RegistryService.py
   Thread the include_simulations flag; status helper skips sims.
4. src/api/routers/internal/domain.py
   run_blocking around load_domain_from_uc so Lakebase I/O does not block the loop.
5. src/front/static/global/js/navbar.js
   rememberLoadedDomainOrClear from load response; navigate immediately;
   clear remembered domain on close.
6. src/front/static/registry/js/registry.js
   home-tasks.js, domain-versions.js: remember loaded domain before navigate.
7. tests/units/domain/test_load_domain_from_uc_perf.py
   Contracts for sims skip / single save / domain payload.
8. tests/units/architecture/baseline.json
   Drop load_domain_from_uc from oversized_functions (now under budget).

