## Move Settings from feature selector into User dropdown
================================================================================

Context: Settings was the admin-only fifth row of the feature selector
(#obAppSwitcher). Users expect Settings with other account utilities, so
it now lives in the User dropdown and is removed from the feature selector.

Changes:

1. src/front/templates/base.html
   Removed the Settings app-switcher row; added admin-gated #navSettingsLink
   in the User dropdown (before Help / Report an issue).
2. src/front/static/global/css/permissions.css
   Dropped the unused .ob-app-switcher-item[data-requires-app="admin"] flex
   restore; dropdown-item admin gate remains for the new Settings link.
3. .cursor/11-frontend-design.mdc
   Documented Settings as user-dropdown-only (not an app-switcher row).
4. docs/user-guide.md
   Updated the Settings navigation instruction to the User dropdown.
5. tests/units/front/test_app_switcher_contract.py
   Feature selector now expects four workspaces and no Settings row.
6. tests/units/front/test_user_menu_contract.py
   Added contract that Settings lives in the User dropdown, not the switcher.
7. tests/units/front/test_backend_brand_icons.py
   Updated the "no top-navbar gear" contract for the user-dropdown link.
8. tests/units/front/test_workspace_home_contract.py
   Renamed/updated admin-only Settings assertions for the user dropdown.
9. tests/units/api/test_ui_rendering.py
   Asserts #navSettingsLink instead of any /settings anchor.
10. tests/e2e/navigation/test_navigation_flows.py
    Updated comment to match the new Settings entry point.

