## Separator under Settings and hide Activity on Home page
================================================================================

Context: In the User dropdown, Settings needed a visual divider separating
it from the general Help / Report issue items below. On the Home page
(the landing Registry surface), the Activity button is not necessary and
caused visual clutter.

Changes:

1. src/front/templates/base.html
   - Added an admin-gated `<hr class="dropdown-divider">` immediately below
     Settings in the User dropdown.
   - Added `id="activityCenterNavItem"` to the Activity Center `<li>` element.
2. src/front/static/global/css/main.css
   - Added rule hiding `#activityCenterNavItem` on `body[data-page="home"]`.
   - Adjusted sibling margin to maintain clean spacing next to User dropdown.
3. .cursor/11-frontend-design.mdc
   - Documented the separator under Settings in the User dropdown.
   - Documented that Activity button is hidden on the Home page.
4. tests/units/front/test_user_menu_contract.py
   - Added test verifying the separator between Settings and Help.
5. tests/units/front/test_activity_center_contract.py
   - Added test verifying Activity Center is hidden on the Home page.
6. tests/units/front/test_workspace_home_contract.py
   - Updated count of admin-gated elements in user dropdown (link + divider).

